 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "From a firm plan to a hope",
     "texto": [
      "With different expressions you show how certain a plan is:\n\n- Decided plan: **voy a** + infinitive, **tengo previsto** + infinitive.\n- Intention: **pienso** + infinitive, **tengo la intención de** + infinitive.\n- Idea you are still considering: **estoy pensando en** + infinitive.\n- Hope: **a ver si** + present.\n\n**En principio** and **si todo va bien** leave the door open to a change.\n\n**Enterarse de que** means to find out some news: **me he enterado de que** te vas. And **ser capaz de** + infinitive means to be able to do something; in the negative it sometimes means not daring: **no soy capaz de** decírselo."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Pensar has three uses",
     "texto": [
      "**Pensar** changes meaning depending on what follows:\n\n- **pensar** + infinitive: to intend. **Pienso viajar** en verano.\n- **pensar en** + something: to have it in mind. **Pienso en** mi familia.\n- **pensar que** + verb: to have an opinion. **Pienso que** es buena idea.\n\nTo say how firm a plan is, from most to least: **voy a**, **tengo previsto**, **pienso**, **estoy pensando en**, **a ver si**."
     ],
